{
  "id": "boolean-operators",
  "title": "Boolean Operators",
  "reflection_prompt": "Look back at a nested-if exercise from the previous unit. How would you rewrite it using and/or instead? Which version is easier to read?",
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "01",
      "source_unit": "boolean-operators",
      "title": "Using and",
      "sidebar_tag": "and",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read two integers, one per line, and print <code>True</code> if",
        "<strong>both</strong> are positive, or <code>False</code> otherwise, using",
        "the <code>and</code> operator.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "3",
        "5",
        "True</pre>",
        "<p><code>and</code> only produces <code>True</code> when both sides of it",
        "are true.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "a = int(input())",
        "b = int(input())",
        "",
        "# TODO: print True if both a and b are positive, otherwise False"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "3",
            "5"
          ],
          "expected": "True"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "3",
            "-5"
          ],
          "expected": "False"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "-3",
            "5"
          ],
          "expected": "False"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "-3",
            "-5"
          ],
          "expected": "False"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "0",
            "5"
          ],
          "expected": "False"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "02",
      "source_unit": "boolean-operators",
      "title": "Using or",
      "sidebar_tag": "or",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read two integers, one per line, and print <code>True</code> if",
        "<strong>at least one</strong> is positive, or <code>False</code> otherwise,",
        "using the <code>or</code> operator.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "-3",
        "5",
        "True</pre>",
        "<p><code>or</code> produces <code>True</code> as long as at least one side",
        "of it is true.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "a = int(input())",
        "b = int(input())",
        "",
        "# TODO: print True if at least one of a, b is positive, otherwise False"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "-3",
            "5"
          ],
          "expected": "True"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "3",
            "-5"
          ],
          "expected": "True"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "-3",
            "-5"
          ],
          "expected": "False"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "3",
            "5"
          ],
          "expected": "True"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "0",
            "0"
          ],
          "expected": "False"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03",
      "source_unit": "boolean-operators",
      "title": "Using not",
      "sidebar_tag": "not",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read an integer and print <code>True</code> if it is",
        "<strong>not</strong> zero, or <code>False</code> if it is zero, using the",
        "<code>not</code> operator.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "5",
        "True</pre>",
        "<p><code>not</code> flips a boolean value: <code>not True</code> is",
        "<code>False</code>, and <code>not False</code> is <code>True</code>.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "n = int(input())",
        "",
        "# TODO: print not (n == 0)"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "5"
          ],
          "expected": "True"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "0"
          ],
          "expected": "False"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "-5"
          ],
          "expected": "True"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "1"
          ],
          "expected": "True"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "-1"
          ],
          "expected": "True"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
