    {
      "id": "07",
      "source_unit": "boolean-operators",
      "title": "Combining and and or",
      "sidebar_tag": "and / or",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read three integers <code>a</code>, <code>b</code>, <code>c</code>, one",
        "per line, and print <code>True</code> if <code>a</code> is positive",
        "<strong>and</strong> either <code>b</code> or <code>c</code> is positive.",
        "Print <code>False</code> otherwise.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "5",
        "-1",
        "3",
        "True</pre>",
        "<p><code>and</code> binds more tightly than <code>or</code> in Python, so",
        "<code>a and b or c</code> is grouped as <code>(a and b) or c</code> &mdash;",
        "not what we want here. Use parentheses to make the grouping explicit:",
        "<code>a and (b or c)</code>.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "a = int(input())",
        "b = int(input())",
        "c = int(input())",
        "",
        "# TODO: print a > 0 and (b > 0 or c > 0)"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "5",
            "-1",
            "3"
          ],
          "expected": "True"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "5",
            "-1",
            "-1"
          ],
          "expected": "False"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "-5",
            "1",
            "1"
          ],
          "expected": "False"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "5",
            "1",
            "1"
          ],
          "expected": "True"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "5",
            "0",
            "0"
          ],
          "expected": "False"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
