      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "yes",
            "1"
          ],
          "expected": "Refund approved"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "no",
            "48"
          ],
          "expected": "Refund approved"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "no",
            "1"
          ],
          "expected": "No refund"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "yes",
            "48"
          ],
          "expected": "Refund approved"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "no",
            "24"
          ],
          "expected": "No refund"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09",
      "source_unit": "boolean-operators",
      "title": "Nested If vs. and: Same Result",
      "sidebar_tag": "and",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read a <code>temp</code> and whether it's <code>raining</code>",
        "(<code>yes</code>/<code>no</code>), and print <code>Snow</code> if it's",
        "below 32 <strong>and</strong> raining, or <code>Not snowing</code>",
        "otherwise.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "20",
        "yes",
        "Snow</pre>",
        "<p>A previous unit handled a similar problem with two levels of nested",
        "<code>if</code> statements. When there are only two conditions and only",
        "one of the four combinations needs special handling, a single",
        "<code>and</code> is usually clearer than nesting.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "temp = int(input())",
        "raining = input()",
        "",
        "# TODO: print \"Snow\" if temp < 32 and raining == \"yes\",",
        "# otherwise \"Not snowing\""
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "20",
            "yes"
          ],
          "expected": "Snow"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "20",
            "no"
          ],
          "expected": "Not snowing"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "60",
            "yes"
          ],
          "expected": "Not snowing"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "60",
            "no"
          ],
          "expected": "Not snowing"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "31",
            "yes"
          ],
          "expected": "Snow"
        }
      ]
    },
